 "final_message": "I applied with Brightpath Home Lending (application BHL-26001), and your intent to proceed is recorded.\n\n- **Lender choice:** Brightpath's 30-year fixed at 6.250% was the lowest rate that fit your limits. Cascade's 6.125% has $19,450 in closing costs, so it fails your limit. Cascade's other option is 6.625%, which is over your rate limit. Summit Ridge's 6.375% fits but is higher than Brightpath's.\n- **Documents shared:** Only with Brightpath. I uploaded the last 2 statements for each of your four personal accounts and the last 2 payslips for each of you. I did not touch Nadia's business checking account.\n- **Application:** I filled it in from your profile and those documents, gave the credit-check and e-sign consents, and submitted it once.\n- **Underwriting condition:** Brightpath asked about the $8,000 deposit on 9/3 into Sam's checking. I asked you, and you said it was a gift from Sam's parents toward the down payment. I sent that as a written explanation.\n- **Loan Estimate:** The rate is 6.250%, the monthly payment is $3,042.41, and closing costs are $12,850. That is within all three of your limits. I signed the intent to proceed with both your names.\n\nThe application status was \"Loan Estimate issued; conditional review\" before I answered the condition. I didn't check the status again afterward, so Brightpath's review of your explanation may still be pending.",
